course: dictionary
lesson: 5895
title: Map: a drawing, a verb, and a plan
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A map is a drawing of an area, such as a room, a town, a country or the world, seen from above. It shows where places are. Context helps you spot which meaning is used: «The coloured paint marks that workers spray on the pavement before roadworks are a map of that hidden city, showing where pipes and cables run.» Here the map shows where things are under the ground.
explain: Map can also be a verb, which means to make a map of a place. Map out is a phrase that means to plan something carefully. If you are not sure, swap in your meaning and check whether the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maps often show scale, which tells you how much detail you can see. «A large-scale map, such as 1:25,000, shows a small area in great detail, while a small-scale map, such as 1:10,000,000, shows a huge area with little detail.» A map with a bigger scale shows less land but more detail.
explain: Sometimes a map is not a real map at all. «But the game prints no scale at all, so you judge distance by how many locations an army marches through, not by kilometres, and a real map is far more exact.» The author compares a game map with a real one, so you can tell that a real map gives you exact distances.
fact: A map is a drawing of an area seen from above, showing where places are.
fact: Maps can have a title, a key, a scale and a compass showing N, E, S and W.
fact: An atlas is a book of maps, and a globe is a round map.
fact: «Map» can also be a verb, meaning to make a map of a place.
fact: «Map out» means to plan something carefully.
exercise: «The coloured paint marks on the pavement are a map of that hidden city.» What is a map in this sentence? | *A drawing showing where pipes and cables run | A kind of hole dug by diggers | A city in a book | A type of paint sprayed on walls
exercise: «A large-scale map shows a small area in great detail.» What does a large-scale map show? | *A small area in great detail | Only the sea | A huge area with little detail | Only the sky
exercise: Which phrase means to plan something carefully? | *Map out | Read a map | World map | Treasure map
test: «A globe is a round map.» What is a globe? | A flat drawing of a room | *A round map | A book of maps | A compass
test: In maths, which word tells you how a map shrinks real distances, such as 1 cm = 1 km? | Compass | Grid reference | *Scale | Key
exam: «We will map out our route before we set off.» What does map out mean here? | To lose your way | To paint a wall | To count the miles | *To plan something carefully
